{
  "uid": "homelab-site-service-health",
  "title": "Sites & Failover \u2014 Which Site Is Each Thing At?",
  "description": "Which site is each service at, and is it up. Every service row carries an explicit Site column. HOME is this k3s cluster and is fully instrumented; Kubernetes objects have no site label of their own, so this dashboard stamps site=\"home\" onto them with label_replace \u2014 a definition, not a measurement. ORACLE runs a separate, non-federated Prometheus and CANADA has no scrape target at all, so both are reported as \"unknown from here\" rather than faked. Both of those panels count targets instead of probing a hard-coded job name, so they start working by themselves once the corresponding scrape job is added. Rebuilt 2026-09-21: the previous Canada panel queried up{job=\"canada-pantry-bot-api\"}, a job present in neither the repo nor the live Prometheus config, so it could only ever render No data. Updated 2026-09-22 (#191): Oracle now remote-writes its series here (site=\"oracle\") and Canada's roles are scraped through Home's relay (site=\"canada\"); Home series carry no site label, so Home-only panels filter site=\"\".",
