    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Every service row below carries an explicit **Site** column, so no panel here requires you to already know where something runs.\n\n> **2026-09-25:** PantryBot was consolidated onto Oracle and the three-site failover design (Home/Oracle/Canada plus a GCP witness) was retired. The Canada site, the failover witness and the fencing panels have been removed from this dashboard because their subjects no longer exist \u2014 an empty panel reads as a fault, which is worse than no panel.\n\n\n| Site | What it is | How this Prometheus sees it |\n|---|---|---|\n| **HOME** | MinecraftMachine, the single-node k3s cluster on the home LAN (192.168.40.208). Since 2026-09-25 it runs **Minecraft and Authentik only** \u2014 PantryBot moved to Oracle. It is kept as a cold restore target: nothing PantryBot-shaped runs here, but the manifests and a pre-cutover database volume remain. | Fully instrumented: kube-state-metrics, cAdvisor, Alloy/Loki. PantryBot microservice scrape jobs here will be down, and that is now correct rather than a fault. |\n| **ORACLE** | Oracle Cloud ARM instance, `pantry-bot-oracle`. **This is where PantryBot runs.** Gateway, worker, dispatcher, overlay, api, private-site and commands-site all serve from here, behind both Cloudflare tunnels. | **Not federated into this Prometheus.** `observability/oracle-prometheus-config.yaml` configures a separate Prometheus on Oracle. Panels below that show Oracle as absent are describing this federation gap, not an outage. |\n| **GREENIE'S PC** | Windows/Docker gaming PC (`ThePantry`) | Reaches this Prometheus via Alloy remote-write as `site=\"windows-remote\"`. Detail on the Greenie's Main PC dashboard. |"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "HOME \u2014 scrape targets up",
      "description": "Targets this Prometheus scrapes that belong to the home cluster.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(up{site=\"home\"} or up{job!~\".*oracle.*\"} unless up{site!=\"\"})",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
